  "methods/kurz.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "Spectrum Probe\\_Folie\\_ATR~\\cite{data-ftir-probe-folie-atr} was evaluated between 3999 and 600~cm$^{-1}$ (3527 data points) with Folio Lab, FTIR module, version <version>~\\cite{folio-lab-ftir}."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "methods/s1.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "Spectrum Probe\\_Folie\\_ATR~\\cite{data-ftir-probe-folie-atr} was evaluated between 3999 and 600~cm$^{-1}$ (3527 data points)."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "methods/s2.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "Processing: Convert to absorbance."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "methods/s3.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "Bands were picked as local maxima with a prominence of at least 2.0~\\% of the data range, at least 10 times the noise and a minimum distance of 8~cm$^{-1}$, and assigned using a correlation table of group frequencies~\\cite{socrates2001,silverstein2014}; among the matching table entries, those whose shape fits the band and whose group is supported by the functional-group rating of the whole spectrum come first."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "methods/s4.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "The assignments are suggestions."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "methods/s5.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "The signal-to-noise ratio is about 353: height of the strongest band (maximum of the spectrum after a 12~cm$^{-1}$ moving mean, above a rubber-band baseline) divided by the standard deviation of the noise, estimated from the residual of a Savitzky-Golay smooth (7 points, cubic)~\\cite{savitzky1964} as a robust standard deviation (1.4826 $\\cdot$ median of the absolute values) over the quiet sections."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "methods/s6.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "The library search (Correlation) compared the spectrum with Modellbibliothek (Folio Lab); sample and references were prepared the same way (absorbance, 2~cm$^{-1}$ grid, rubber-band baseline, maximum 1), the processing steps above apply to the sample only."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "methods/s7.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "The hit quality index HQI ranges from 0 to 100."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "methods/s8.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "The model library~\\cite{folio-ftir-modell} contains references calculated from literature band positions, not measured spectra; its hits are indications."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
