  "text-ergebnisse.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "The spectrum of Probe\\_Folie\\_ATR shows \\labval{ftir-probe-folie-atr}{npeaks} bands; the strongest are at 1715, 1242, 1095, 1018, 724~cm$^{-1}$. The band positions indicate: Aromatic ring, Ester. No O--H/N--H band: no alcohol, water, primary/secondary amine or amide. No triple bond (C$\\equiv$N, C$\\equiv$C) and no isocyanate. The best library hit is \\labval{ftir-probe-folie-atr}{hit1} with an HQI of \\labval{ftir-probe-folie-atr}{hqi1}."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "text-methodik.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "Spectrum Probe\\_Folie\\_ATR~\\cite{data-ftir-probe-folie-atr} was evaluated between 3999 and 600~cm$^{-1}$ (3527 data points). Processing: Convert to absorbance. Bands were picked as local maxima with a prominence of at least 2.0~\\% of the data range, at least 10 times the noise and a minimum distance of 8~cm$^{-1}$, and assigned using a correlation table of group frequencies~\\cite{socrates2001,silverstein2014}; among the matching table entries, those whose shape fits the band and whose group is supported by the functional-group rating of the whole spectrum come first. The assignments are suggestions. The signal-to-noise ratio is about 353: height of the strongest band (maximum of the spectrum after a 12~cm$^{-1}$ moving mean, above a rubber-band baseline) divided by the standard deviation of the noise, estimated from the residual of a Savitzky-Golay smooth (7 points, cubic)~\\cite{savitzky1964} as a robust standard deviation (1.4826 $\\cdot$ median of the absolute values) over the quiet sections. The library search (Correlation) compared the spectrum with Modellbibliothek (Folio Lab); sample and references were prepared the same way (absorbance, 2~cm$^{-1}$ grid, rubber-band baseline, maximum 1), the processing steps above apply to the sample only. The hit quality index HQI ranges from 0 to 100. The model library~\\cite{folio-ftir-modell} contains references calculated from literature band positions, not measured spectra; its hits are indications."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
